   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import os\n",
    "\n",
    "os.environ[\"GOOGLE_API_KEY\"] = \Google-API\""
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 7,
   "id": "93685ec9-ad20-4c36-ba95-4afc20292961",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "from typing import TypedDict\n",
    "from langgraph.graph import StateGraph, END\n",
    "from langchain_google_genai import ChatGoogleGenerativeAI\n",
    "from langchain_core.messages import HumanMessage\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 8,
   "id": "a65bd451-6fc2-422b-b22b-5ae101e1a3d1",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "class AgentState(TypedDict):\n",
    "    user_input: str\n",
    "    agent_response: str\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 9,
   "id": "279bc116-080b-4b36-bdd2-51a5c7f1c6e4",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "llm = ChatGoogleGenerativeAI(\n",
    "    model=\"gemini-3-flash-preview\",\n",
    "    temperature=0\n",
    ")\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 10,
   "id": "32900f41-db0c-45c0-90b1-6968a9794fe4",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "def agent_node(state: AgentState) -> AgentState:\n",
    "    response = llm.invoke([\n",
    "        HumanMessage(content=state[\"user_input\"])\n",
    "    ])\n",
    "\n",
    "    if isinstance(response.content, list):\n",
    "        text = \"\".join(\n",
    "            block[\"text\"] for block in response.content\n",
    "            if block.get(\"type\") == \"text\"\n",
    "        )\n",
    "    else:\n",
    "        text = response.content\n",
    "\n",
    "    return {\n",
    "        \"user_input\": state[\"user_input\"],\n",
    "        \"agent_response\": text\n",
    "    }\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 11,
   "id": "d841ae16-e1d4-4c81-b331-570640536c18",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "graph = StateGraph(AgentState)\n",
    "\n",
    "graph.add_node(\"agent\", agent_node)\n",
    "graph.set_entry_point(\"agent\")\n",
    "graph.add_edge(\"agent\", END)\n",
    "\n",
    "app = graph.compile()\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 12,
   "id": "8b7cd696-ce50-4efe-ae69-26bacc791f6b",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "Think of **LangGraph** as a way to give an AI a **flowchart** to follow.\n",
      "\n",
      "While standard AI usually works in a straight line (Input $\\rightarrow$ Process $\\rightarrow$ Output), LangGraph allows the AI to **loop back**, double-check its work, and coordinate between different \"specialist\" AIs.\n",
      "\n",
      "Here is the breakdown in simple terms:\n",
      "\n",
      "---\n",
      "\n",
      "### 1. The Problem: AI is usually a \"One-Way Street\"\n",
      "Most AI tools (like basic LangChain) work in a linear sequence:\n",
      "*   **Step 1:** Search the web.\n",
      "*   **Step 2:** Summarize the info.\n",
      "*   **Step 3:** Give the answer.\n",
      "\n",
      "But what if the search results were bad? In a linear system, the AI just gives you a bad summary. It can't \"go back\" and try again.\n",
      "\n",
      "### 2. The Solution: LangGraph (The Flowchart)\n",
      "LangGraph turns that straight line into a **map with loops**. It uses three main concepts:\n",
      "\n",
      "*   **Nodes (The Workers):** Think of these as specific steps or people. One node is a \"Researcher,\" another is a \"Writer,\" and another is a \"Fact-Checker.\"\n",
      "*   **Edges (The Paths):** These are the arrows connecting the workers. They tell the AI where to go next.\n",
      "*   **State (The Shared Clipboard):** This is a shared memory. Every worker can see what has been done so far, add to it, and pass it to the next person.\n",
      "\n",
      "### 3. The \"Superpower\": Cycles (Looping)\n",
      "The biggest reason people use LangGraph is for **Cycles**. \n",
      "\n",
      "Imagine you ask an AI to write code. \n",
      "1.  **Node A** writes the code.\n",
      "2.  **Node B** tests the code.\n",
      "3.  **The Edge (The Logic):** If the code has an error, the arrow points **back** to Node A to fix it. If it works, the arrow points to the user.\n",
      "\n",
      "**This \"looping until it's right\" is what LangGraph makes possible.**\n",
      "\n",
      "---\n",
      "\n",
      "### A Real-World Example: An AI Travel Agent\n",
      "If you used a standard AI, it might suggest a hotel that is actually sold out because it only checked once. \n",
      "\n",
      "With **LangGraph**, the flow looks like this:\n",
      "1.  **Search Node:** Finds a hotel.\n",
      "2.  **Check Node:** Tries to \"book\" it.\n",
      "3.  **Decision Point:** \n",
      "    *   Is it available? $\\rightarrow$ Go to **Final Confirmation**.\n",
      "    *   Is it sold out? $\\rightarrow$ **Loop back** to the Search Node to find a different one.\n",
      "\n",
      "### Summary: Why does it matter?\n",
      "*   **Better Accuracy:** The AI can fact-check itself and correct errors before talking to you.\n",
      "*   **Complex Tasks:** It can handle big projects that require many steps and \"if/then\" logic.\n",
      "*   **Persistence:** LangGraph can \"save\" the state. If the AI gets interrupted, it remembers exactly where it was on the flowchart and can resume later.\n",
      "\n",
      "**In short: LangGraph turns a simple AI chatbot into a reliable, multi-step AI workforce.**\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "result = app.invoke({\n",
    "    \"user_input\": \"Explain LangGraph in simple terms\",\n",
    "    \"agent_response\": \"\"\n",
    "})\n",
    "\n",
    "print(result[\"agent_response\"])\n"
   ]
  },
